# Repository Rules — MASS-GT (tfs-harmony)

## Code placement
- ALL Python package code belongs under `src/mass_gt/`.
- Do not add new top-level modules to `src/` (e.g. don't create `src/foo.py`).

## Paths & configuration
- All filesystem paths MUST come from `mass_gt.config` (BASE_DIR, DATA_DIR,
  INPUT_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR, DIMENSIONS_DIR).
- Never hardcode paths or read environment variables directly; go through
  `mass_gt.config`.
- Configuration is loaded via python-dotenv; the local `.env` file is
  git-ignored (copy from `.env.example`).

## Calculation code (hard constraint)
- Mathematical / stochastic models (random draws, FRATAR scaling, tour
  formation, traffic assignment, emission calculations) MUST remain STRICTLY
  UNALTERED.
- Any refactor is additive: wrap, never rewrite. Golden-file baseline outputs
  must be reproduced before and after changes.
- The `varDict` configuration contract consumed by the modules is frozen.

## Workflow
- Keep commits small and focused on a single concern.
- Never force-push to shared branches.
- Private / proprietary data must never enter the repository.